course: dictionary
lesson: 6957
title: Palestinian: a word for people and places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Palestinian can be an adjective or a noun. As an adjective, it describes things connected with the Palestinian people, such as «Palestinian food». As a noun, a Palestinian is a person from this people, whether they live in the Middle East or somewhere else in the world.
explain: The Palestinian territories are the West Bank and the Gaza Strip, both in the Middle East. Gaza is a small, crowded strip of land by the sea, home to about two million Palestinians. Look at a map: the West Bank is inland, and Gaza is by the sea.
explain: Some news is about a long, painful conflict over land, safety and rights. Many points are still disputed, so it is fair to hear each side's view in its own words. Both Palestinian and Israeli families have suffered, and you can feel for both at the same time.
fact: Palestinian is an adjective («Palestinian food») and a noun («a Palestinian»).
fact: «Palestinian people» means people from or connected with the Palestinian people.
fact: The Palestinian territories are the West Bank and the Gaza Strip, in the Middle East.
fact: Palestinian food such as hummus, falafel and maqluba is enjoyed around the world.
fact: In Roman and later times, the region was called Palestine in history books.
exercise: «Palestinian food such as hummus and falafel is enjoyed around the world.» In this sentence, what kind of word is Palestinian? | A place name only | A noun, meaning a person | A verb, meaning to eat | *An adjective, describing the food
exercise: As a noun, what does «a Palestinian» mean? | A type of bread only | *A person from the Palestinian people, wherever they live | A river in the Middle East | A town in Europe
exercise: Which two places are the Palestinian territories? | *The West Bank and the Gaza Strip | The Mediterranean Sea and the Atlantic Ocean | London and Paris | The Jordan River and the Nile
test: Ahmed is a Palestinian. In this sentence, what is Ahmed? | A place in the Middle East | *A person from the Palestinian people | A kind of food | A river
test: Which one is a Palestinian territory? | Egypt | The Jordan River | The Mediterranean Sea | *The West Bank
exam: Why is it fair to hear each side's view in its own words when reading about the Palestinian and Israeli conflict? | Because one side is always right | *Because many points are disputed and both peoples have suffered | Because it is quicker than reading a map | Because the news is never true
